  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Accommodation Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a reasonable accommodation request form?\", \"a\": \"It is the document an employee or job applicant uses to ask for a change at work because of a disability. A typical ADA accommodation request form asks which job tasks are affected and what change would help.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a reasonable accommodation request form for employees?\", \"a\": \"Decide who receives requests first, then write questions about the affected task and the change being asked for, with no diagnosis field. Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a> turns that description into a working form that sends requests straight to HR and keeps a dated log of each case.\"}, {\"q\": \"What fields does a reasonable accommodation request form need?\", \"a\": \"Five cover most cases: the person's name and job title, the task that has become difficult, the change being requested, how long it is needed, and how they prefer to be contacted. Leave out diagnosis and medical history. If documentation is ever needed, it comes later through a separate request.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where can employers find a reasonable accommodation request form template?\", \"a\": \"The Job Accommodation Network posts sample forms employers can adapt, and many state agencies and universities publish the version they give their own staff. Whichever you start from, link it in your new employee form packet so new hires know where it lives.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can an employer accept a request for accommodation without an ADA form?\", \"a\": \"Yes, and it has to. EEOC guidance says a request can be spoken and needs no special wording. An employer may ask the person to confirm it on a form afterward. It cannot set the request aside while that paperwork is pending.\"}, {\"q\": \"What types of changes can an ADA accommodation request form cover?\", \"a\": \"Common ones are a modified schedule, new equipment or screen reading software, an interpreter, reassignment to a vacant position, and leave. Leave can start on the <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/time-off-request-form'>time off request form</a>. An employer may offer a different change that works just as well, and can refuse to provide any effective accommodation only when every option would cause undue hardship.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should an ADA accommodation form include a doctor's note?\", \"a\": \"No. Keep medical questions off the request itself. EEOC guidance lets an employer ask for documentation when the disability or the need for the change is not obvious. That letter can come from any appropriate health care or rehabilitation professional, not only a physician, and it is filed confidentially, away from the personnel folder.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can an ADA accommodation request form be filled out online?\", \"a\": \"Yes. The ADA sets no paper requirement, even though many agencies still post their ADA accommodation request form as a PDF to print and sign. An online version reaches HR the moment it is sent. Emergent builds that version on a database you own, with no cap on responses.\"}, {\"q\": \"How does HR track ADA accommodation request forms?\", \"a\": \"One case per request works best: the date it arrived, each meeting in the interactive process, the options weighed, and the written decision with its start date. A shared inbox loses that thread quickly. Emergent can build the case log from a plain-English description, including a reminder when a case sits untouched.\"}, {\"q\": \"Do federal agencies use a different reasonable accommodation request form?\", \"a\": \"Usually, yes. Executive Order 13164 requires every federal agency to keep written reasonable accommodation procedures, and many attach a request form of their own. A federal employee can still ask orally or in writing, including through a supervisor. A denial has to come in writing with the specific reasons.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
